          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"hamsun-victoria-7363807c39cdd645\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.95,\"analysis\":\"The old gentleman directly avows that he loves his wife even more now than before, elaborating the truth-conditional claim through comparison with their first meeting and gratitude for their life together. The response weakly reaffirms their marital bond, but it contains no clear promise or undertaking, so performative support is slight. Repetition and visible emotion intensify the avowal but do not independently establish expressive/reflexive force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"There is weak performative shading because the reassurance renews relational solidarity, but its explicit content primarily describes enduring present love rather than undertaking a future obligation.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Direct speech by the old gentleman to his wife within the embedded exemplary love story narrated by the monk Vendt.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The wife fears that paralysis and disfigurement have made her unlovable. Her husband answers with an emphatic, retrospective avowal that rejects her premise and affirms that his love has increased. His subsequent self-disfigurement strongly corroborates the tale's presentation of radical devotion, though that later action does not convert the core declaration itself into a clear undertaking. The repetitions and his being red with emotion mark intensity, not independently reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg, jeg elsker dig mere, mere end mit liv” (“I, I love you more, more than my life”).\",\"supports\":\"A maximally explicit present-state avowal, strongly supporting T; repetition supplies emphasis but not by itself E.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"He says he loves her as on the first day and then adds, “Men endnu mere elsker jeg dig nu” (“But I love you even more now”).\",\"supports\":\"The temporal comparison and explicit present-tense claim reinforce truth-conditional presentation of continuing love.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The declaration answers her fear that he “cannot love” her as before after she has become paralyzed and believes herself ugly.\",\"supports\":\"The utterance functions chiefly as a corrective avowal and reassurance; the context gives only weak support for relational reaffirmation as P.\",\"confidence\":0.97},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The gentleman embraces her “rød av bevægelse” (“red with emotion”) before answering, but proceeds through an extended recollection of the rose, her eyes, and their shared years.\",\"supports\":\"The delivery is deeply emotional, yet the passage does not portray the words as involuntarily blurted or reflexively discharged; this supports E=0.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Afterward he disfigures his own face with acid, placing himself in a condition analogous to hers.\",\"supports\":\"The later deed contextually corroborates extraordinary devotion and sincerity, while remaining distinct from the core utterance's force.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e6\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is from Knut Hamsun's Victoria, near relative position 0.901, and is identified as a valid explicit first-person love declaration.\",\"supports\":\"Identifies and locates the classified occurrence without altering its T/P/E analysis.\",\"confidence\":1.0}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the central avowal, with slight P support for relational reaffirmation. Emotional intensity is adequately treated as contextual delivery rather than E, and no important core-force residue requires O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
